message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "movilidad-foranea: Intercity Mobility & Hotel Geolocation Web Scraping System"
# TODO: change for the real abstract 
abstract: >-
  This paper develops a methodology to extract, organise and structure spatial data on intercity mobility and hotel infrastructure in Mexico from web platforms. Five independent Python scripts automate queries to bus operators, ticket aggregators and an accommodation reservation platform. The architecture separates input parameters, platform-specific extraction and structured outputs, combining browser automation with network traffic interception to recover accommodation coordinates. A spatial subdivision strategy retrieves establishments beyond those displayed in the initial map query. Applied to ten Mexican cities selected for their demographic or tourism relevance,
  the workflow generates platform-specific databases. Subsequent processing in R produces an origin–destination matrix of aggregated platform records and a georeferenced accommodation database, illustrated through flow maps and kernel density surfaces. The contribution is methodological: a documented architecture connecting web queries to spatial datasets. The outputs represent visible platform supply rather than observed passenger movements or exhaustive service inventories.

